{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.OptionE.CrystalGraph","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule_third_rung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule_third_rung","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L101-L114","doc":"**Verification**: the depth-based rule assigns rung 3 to the third vertex\n(idx 2), continuing the `source_rung` / `second_rung` pattern.\n\nNOTE: on the current **placeholder** depth function `k v := v.idx + 1` this\nholds for every `Γ`; the previous `depthBasedRule_reaches_k3` carried an\n**unused** `h : 3 ≤ Γ.vertexCount` and a \"k ≥ 3 reach property\" docstring it\ndid not establish. The substantive \"substrate-derived k ≥ 3\" content — that\nthe *concrete* crystal-graph depth reaches 3 below the k = 2 horizon — is the\nopen Option-E goal (property 2 in the header), not this placeholder unfolding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule_second_rung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule_second_rung","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L94-L99","doc":"The depth-based rule assigns rung 2 to vertex with idx 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule_source_rung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule_source_rung","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L86-L92","doc":"**Verification**: the depth-based rule assigns rung 1 to the\nsource vertex (idx 0), rung 2 to the next, etc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.depthBasedRule","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L77-L83","doc":"**Candidate rule (depth-based)**: for each vertex `v`, the\nrung `k(v)` is the depth of `v` in the crystal graph,\ncounted from the source. The depth function is defined\nabstractly here; concrete values come from per-partition\ncrystal-graph data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.RungRule.k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.RungRule.k","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The rung assignment: vertex → rung index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.RungRule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.RungRule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.RungRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptionE.RungSelection.RungRule","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OptionE/RungSelection.lean#L48-L75","doc":"**Canonical rung-selection function** signature: given a\ncrystal vertex, return its canonical rung index.\n\n**`substrate_derived : Prop` removed 2026-09-14, and NOT replaced by a\nparameter.** It was typed with the *universe* `Prop`, so the constructor\nchose the proposition — `depthBasedRule` supplied `True` — and it was\nmeasured dead: written once, read by nothing inside this file or outside\nit.\n\n**The property it named is not expressible in this type at all, which is\nwhy parameterising would not have helped.** It read: *\"the rule does not\ndirectly reference any real-valued AME constant.\"* That is a statement\nabout how `k` is **defined**, not about `k` as a function — two\nextensionally equal functions can differ entirely in provenance, and Lean\nsees only the extension. No field, and no caller-supplied predicate on\n`k`, can carry it.\n\nIts honest home is a **provenance audit over the source**, which this\ncorpus already does elsewhere: `scripts/precision-gates.sh` runs a\nno-free-parameter certificate of exactly that shape. The Option-E\nanti-fit discipline for this rule belongs there, not here.\n\nNothing else changes: the field's removal keeps `RungRule n`'s arity, so\n`DeltaLambda`, `DeuteronVerification` and `CrystalDeltaLambdaScaffold` are\nuntouched. ","signatureChunk":0}]}